course: dictionary
lesson: 14052
title: Maritime: connected with the sea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Maritime is an adjective. It describes things that have to do with the sea, ships and sailing. Look at the words around it: if the sentence mentions boats, harbours or sailors, maritime probably means connected with the sea.
explain: «The maritime museum had old maps and a ship's wheel.» A museum with maps and a ship's wheel is about the sea, so maritime means connected with the sea and sailing. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the sea museum had old maps" still makes sense.
explain: Maritime can also describe land near the sea. «Ireland has a mild, wet maritime climate.» Here maritime means near the sea. The sea keeps the land from getting very hot or very cold, so the weather stays mild.
fact: Maritime means connected with the sea, ships and sailing.
fact: Maritime can also mean near the sea or living by the sea.
fact: A maritime climate is mild and wet because the sea keeps the land from getting very hot or very cold.
fact: Ireland and New Zealand both have maritime climates.
fact: «The Maritimes» is a name for three east-coast provinces of Canada: Nova Scotia, New Brunswick and Prince Edward Island.
exercise: «The sailors checked the ropes before the maritime journey.» What does maritime mean here? | Made of wood | Connected with mountains and hills | Very hot and dry | *Connected with ships and sailing
exercise: Why is a maritime climate mild? | The sun is always very close | The wind blows hot air from the desert | *The sea keeps the land from getting very hot or very cold | The land is covered in ice all year
exercise: «The maritime museum shows boats, maps and sailors' tools.» What is the museum about? | Farming and animals | *The sea, ships and sailing | Trains and cars | Dinosaurs and fossils
test: «Our family lives in a maritime town, so we eat a lot of fish.» What does maritime mean? | Covered in snow | *Near the sea | Very high up in the mountains | Far from any water
test: What is a maritime nation? | A country with no coastline at all | *A country that is connected with the sea | A country where people use the sea for travel and trade | A country with only mountains and deserts
exam: «The Maritimes are three provinces on Canada's east coast.» What are the Maritimes? | Three mountain ranges | Three big cities in the desert | *Three east-coast provinces | Three islands in the Pacific
